      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im working on a new pilot and i want to make sure i'm not accidentally leaning too hard into tropes. i have a few character bios drafted and i need a professional eye. can u look at these and tell me if any of them feel like clichés? also, based on their vibes, which ones do u think fit better in a gritty urban crime drama vs a high-society prestige drama?\n\nCharacter A: Marcus, 30s, very observant, always seems to know what's happening in the room before anyone else. \nCharacter B: Julian, 50s, extremely polished, commands respect the moment he walks into a room.\nCharacter C: Li, 20s, incredibly disciplined, high attention to detail, moves with a lot of precision.\nCharacter D: Elena, 40s, elegant, manages a complex social circle with ease.\nCharacter E: Andre, 25, street smart, knows how to navigate difficult environments and tough crowds.\n\ndo these feel like real people or just archetypes? and which genres do they lean toward?",
